1
00:00:06,703 --> 00:00:11,437
Look at a cup. At once it becomes
a handle, a rim and a body.

2
00:00:12,241 --> 00:00:17,786
Cognition divides. It takes a whole,
separates it into parts, and names them.

3
00:00:17,866 --> 00:00:21,128
It asks which part carries
the identity of the whole.

4
00:00:21,208 --> 00:00:24,009
Motion becomes a before and an after.

5
00:00:24,089 --> 00:00:27,120
The Buddhist traditions have
names for this mode of mind:

6
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,769
vikalpa, or kalpanā.

7
00:00:29,849 --> 00:00:34,190
Conceptual construction: the
mind that divides and names.

8
00:00:34,997 --> 00:00:40,080
Nāgārjuna's verses on the Middle
Way answer this habit with analysis.

9
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:45,813
They take motion, fire and fuel, agent
and action, and everything conditioned.

10
00:00:45,893 --> 00:00:50,678
They divide each, and show that none of
the divisions yields what was claimed.

11
00:00:50,758 --> 00:00:54,672
The chariot is not in the
wheels, the axle or the pole.

12
00:00:54,752 --> 00:00:56,574
Motion is not in the mover.

13
00:00:56,654 --> 00:01:00,424
The analysis turns the
dividing mind against itself.

14
00:01:01,233 --> 00:01:03,299
Analysis has two faces.

15
00:01:03,379 --> 00:01:06,710
In thought, it separates
an object into pieces,

16
00:01:06,790 --> 00:01:09,563
and searches for the one
that carries identity.

17
00:01:09,643 --> 00:01:13,141
In perception, the division
is already built in:

18
00:01:13,244 --> 00:01:16,044
we see a cup as parts
because we have learned to.

19
00:01:16,124 --> 00:01:20,460
The verses claim that this way of cutting
things up is not a neutral description of

20
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:23,068
what is there. It is a mode of knowing.

21
00:01:23,148 --> 00:01:26,723
It treats the parts as the
real basis of appearance,

22
00:01:26,803 --> 00:01:29,744
and the whole as a heap
that needs explaining.

23
00:01:30,578 --> 00:01:32,903
The regress makes this visible.

24
00:01:32,983 --> 00:01:34,928
Each part can be divided again.

25
00:01:35,008 --> 00:01:38,664
The search for an indivisible
basis either never ends,

26
00:01:38,744 --> 00:01:42,333
or ends in a part that cannot
be found when it is examined.

27
00:01:42,413 --> 00:01:47,074
Nāgārjuna does not conclude that
ordinary objects are unreal.

28
00:01:47,154 --> 00:01:51,993
He concludes that analysis cannot
find the intrinsic nature it assumed:

29
00:01:52,073 --> 00:01:54,860
a nature a thing would
have from its own side.

30
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,550
The parts, too, are designated.

31
00:01:57,630 --> 00:02:00,435
They are named, and
known through the naming.

32
00:02:01,241 --> 00:02:04,476
So analysis is used to expose analysis.

33
00:02:04,556 --> 00:02:08,787
The dividing mind is shown to
be a formation, not a discovery.

34
00:02:09,610 --> 00:02:12,479
One verse names the
middle way in these terms.

35
00:02:12,559 --> 00:02:16,731
Whatever is dependent co-arising,
that is what we call emptiness.

36
00:02:16,811 --> 00:02:20,581
That, being dependent
designation, is the middle way.

37
00:02:21,398 --> 00:02:23,873
The verse holds three things together.

38
00:02:23,953 --> 00:02:28,873
Dependent arising is the fact that
things come from causes and conditions.

39
00:02:28,953 --> 00:02:33,547
Emptiness is the lack of intrinsic
nature that follows from that fact.

40
00:02:33,627 --> 00:02:37,419
Designation is the way such
things are named and known,

41
00:02:37,499 --> 00:02:39,892
and the naming is itself dependent.

42
00:02:39,972 --> 00:02:44,226
So dependent designation is not a
compromise between existence and

43
00:02:44,306 --> 00:02:49,312
non-existence. It is what the middle
path looks like, once it is understood.

44
00:02:50,117 --> 00:02:52,686
The verse blocks two errors at once.

45
00:02:52,766 --> 00:02:57,510
Eternalism treats things as having a
fixed nature that stands on its own,

46
00:02:57,590 --> 00:02:59,140
whatever the conditions.

47
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:02,795
Nihilism concludes, from
the absence of that nature,

48
00:03:02,875 --> 00:03:04,616
that nothing exists.

49
00:03:04,696 --> 00:03:06,685
Designation avoids both.

50
00:03:06,788 --> 00:03:10,702
Things are not nothing, because
they function and can be named.

51
00:03:10,782 --> 00:03:15,240
They do not exist in themselves,
because their naming depends on causes,

52
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:18,261
on parts, and on the mind that names them.

53
00:03:19,065 --> 00:03:21,512
The logic runs in one direction.

54
00:03:21,592 --> 00:03:25,792
Whatever arises dependently
comes from causes and conditions.

55
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:28,958
Something with intrinsic
nature would need nothing else.

56
00:03:29,038 --> 00:03:32,735
So whatever arises dependently
lacks intrinsic nature.

57
00:03:32,815 --> 00:03:35,266
And that lack is what "empty" means.

58
00:03:36,085 --> 00:03:40,760
Emptiness, then, is not a
separate reality behind phenomena.

59
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:45,371
It is what dependent arising amounts
to, when its status is examined.

60
00:03:46,182 --> 00:03:49,336
There is not one thing that
has not arisen dependently.

61
00:03:49,416 --> 00:03:52,031
And so there is not one
thing that is not empty.

